#idx("Formation lessons")#idx("Wingman")Phase 4 of the training course, Formation and flight lead, is the one phase that flies with other jets of your flight. Its six #term("lesson", shown: "lessons") are the same in the F-16D Barak, the F-16I Sufa and the F-35I Adir, each from its home base. In the F-16s the instructor rides in your back seat; in the F-35I the instructor flies the lead's jet, or your wingman's when you lead. Each jet's flight manual describes how to fly in formation; the briefing of each lesson gives its steps.

#grid-table(
  (auto, auto, 1fr),
  ([Lesson], [You fly], [What you do]),
  [4.1 Wingman], [Kidon 1-2], [a formation take-off beside the lead, fingertip, close up, trail and the rejoin, the landing behind the lead],
  [4.2 Tactical formation], [Kidon 1-2], [line abreast 1,500 m from the lead, its tac turns and its in-place turn],
  [4.3 Lead a pair], [Kidon 1-1], [the #term("tower", shown: "tower") for the pair, a formation take-off, your orders to your wingman, the pair's landing],
  [4.4 Lead a four-ship], [Kidon 1-1], [a stream take-off, the four-ship's formations, the landing in order],
  [4.5 At night], [Kidon 1-2], [lesson 4.1 after dark, on the lead's lights],
  [Check ride 4], [Kidon 1-3], [a four-ship: number 3 on the lead and the lead of your own wingman, Kidon 1-4],
)

=== How the lessons are graded <formation-grades>

#idx("Formation lessons, grades")The briefing lists each lesson's graded items with their standards.

#grid-table(
  (auto, 1fr),
  ([Item], [What counts]),
  [Distance from the formation slot], [the mean distance from your slot, counted once you are within 50 m of it after each order, leaving out the tactical turns],
  [Rejoin time], [from the lead's "rejoin" to your first second within 50 m of your slot],
  [Flight commands given], [the share of the lesson's orders you gave],
  [Every jet of the flight landed], [every jet of the flight down when you are back],
)

A lesson ends when you are parked with the engine off and every jet of the flight has landed.

=== Check ride 4 <formation-check>

#idx("Check ride 4")Check ride 4 grades the formation items above and every item of phases 1 to 3. The instructor gives the briefing and the #term("debrief", shown: "debrief") only: no calls in flight and no switch highlights; the #term("notebook", shown: "notebook") stays open to you. One emergency you have already been taught may come at any time, unannounced.
